From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:34:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegation): queue background calls over a per-chat cap

delegation.at_capacity (sync = off, queue): a background delegate_task that finds the async pool full was run synchronously in the parent's turn, so the chat could not answer or take steers until it ended, and the pool was shared by every chat of the process. With queue, delegation.max_concurrent_children caps each chat's own background units (delegation.max_concurrent_children_total, 0 = none, caps the process), and a call over a cap returns at once with status queued and starts when its chat (or the process) frees a slot, oldest first. Queued units are listed (queue_position) and their children are in the subagent registry as queued: a steer joins the goal when the child starts, a stop settles it as interrupted without running. A graceful restart hands a queued unit off whole, and the next gateway queues it again.
